// Shared mail and social services work without the default player class.
@nonprogrammer
% whisper hello there to #102
=You whisper, "hello there" to Test Programmer.
@programmer
; return 1;
1
=Test Game Player whispers, "hello there"

@nonprogrammer
% page #102 with a private hello
=Your message has been sent.
@programmer
; return 1;
1
=You sense that Test Game Player is looking for you in Test Chamber.
=It pages, "a private hello"

@wizard
; return $mail_agent:send_message(player, {#108}, "Game mail", {"Shared mail works."});
{1, #108}
@nonprogrammer
; return 1;
~~You have new mail
~~Type `help mail'
% @read 1
~~Message 1:
~~Date:
~~From:
~~To:
~~Subject:  Game mail
=
=Shared mail works.
~~---

% @gag #102
~~gagging
@programmer
% say hidden speech
=You say, "hidden speech"
@nonprogrammer
% say my own speech
=You say, "my own speech"
% @ungag #102
~~removed from gag list.
~~gagging

% @refuse page whisper
~~Refusal of
@programmer
; return 1;
1
=Test Game Player says, "my own speech"
% page #108 with should be refused
=Test Game Player refuses your page.
% whisper should be refused to #108
=Test Game Player refuses your whisper.
